    <!-- ==========================================================================
         HOW IT WORKS: 4-STEP LICENSING ROADMAP IN OHIO
         ========================================================================== -->
    <section id="how-it-works" class="py-16 lg:py-20 bg-white border-b border-zinc-200/80">
      <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        
        <div class="text-center max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-12">
          <span class="text-xs font-extrabold uppercase tracking-widest text-orange-600">Ohio Driver Guide</span>
          <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-zinc-950 mt-1">
            4 Simple Steps to Getting Your Ohio License
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm sm:text-base text-zinc-600">
            Here is the clear roadmap from temporary permit to officially holding your Ohio driver's license.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-6">
          
          <!-- Step 1 -->
          <div class="bg-[#FAFAFA] p-6 rounded-2xl border border-zinc-200 relative">
            <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-orange-500 text-white font-black text-base flex items-center justify-center mb-4 shadow-sm">
              01
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-zinc-950 mb-2">Get Your Temp Permit (TIPIC)</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed">
              At age 15½ or older, study the Ohio Digest of Motor Vehicles, take your knowledge and vision test at any Ohio BMV Exam Station, and obtain your Temporary Instruction Permit.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Step 2 -->
          <div class="bg-[#FAFAFA] p-6 rounded-2xl border border-zinc-200 relative">
            <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-orange-500 text-white font-black text-base flex items-center justify-center mb-4 shadow-sm">
              02
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-zinc-950 mb-2">Complete 24 Hours Classroom</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed">
              Enroll in Canal Driving School's online course or attend live classes. You will learn traffic regulations, defensive driving strategies, right-of-way rules, and hazard mitigation.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Step 3 -->
          <div class="bg-[#FAFAFA] p-6 rounded-2xl border border-zinc-200 relative">
            <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-orange-500 text-white font-black text-base flex items-center justify-center mb-4 shadow-sm">
              03
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-zinc-950 mb-2">Complete 8 Hours In-Car</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed">
              Complete four 2-hour behind-the-wheel sessions with our certified instructors. Practice road driving, highway handling, and the Ohio 5-cone maneuverability exam course.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Step 4 -->
          <div class="bg-[#FAFAFA] p-6 rounded-2xl border border-zinc-200 relative">
            <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-orange-500 text-white font-black text-base flex items-center justify-center mb-4 shadow-sm">
              04
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-zinc-950 mb-2">Pass Your Ohio BMV Road Test</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed">
              Receive your Certificate of Completion, complete 50 hours of family practice (including 10 at night), schedule your BMV exam, and earn your official Ohio driver's license!
            </p>
          </div>

        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ==========================================================================
         FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS (FAQS)
         ========================================================================== -->
    <section id="faq" class="py-16 bg-[#FAFAFA] border-b border-zinc-200/80">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        
        <div class="text-center max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-10">
          <div class="w-12 h-1.5 bg-orange-500 rounded-full mx-auto mb-3"></div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold text-zinc-950">
            Frequently Asked Questions
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm sm:text-base text-zinc-600">
            Have questions about our programs or Ohio driving laws? Find clear answers below.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-4">
          
          <details class="group bg-white p-5 rounded-2xl border border-zinc-200 shadow-sm [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
            <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer font-bold text-zinc-950 text-base">
              <span>At what age can my teen begin driving school in Ohio?</span>
              <span class="ml-4 flex-shrink-0 transition duration-300 group-open:-rotate-180 text-orange-600">
                <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
              </span>
            </summary>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed border-t border-zinc-100 pt-3">
              In Ohio, teens can begin classroom or online driver education at exactly <strong>15 years and 6 months of age</strong>. To begin the in-car behind-the-wheel portion, the student must have taken and passed the knowledge test at the BMV to hold a valid Ohio Temporary Instruction Permit Identification Card (TIPIC).
            </p>
          </details>

          <details class="group bg-white p-5 rounded-2xl border border-zinc-200 shadow-sm [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
            <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer font-bold text-zinc-950 text-base">
              <span>Can I take the 24-hour classroom portion online and do in-car lessons with Canal Driving School?</span>
              <span class="ml-4 flex-shrink-0 transition duration-300 group-open:-rotate-180 text-orange-600">
                <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
              </span>
            </summary>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed border-t border-zinc-100 pt-3">
              <strong>Yes!</strong> That is one of our most popular paths. You can complete your 24-hour course online at home and enroll in our 8-hour Behind-the-Wheel Only program. Once you complete both, we issue your official Ohio Certificate of Completion.
            </p>
          </details>

          <details class="group bg-white p-5 rounded-2xl border border-zinc-200 shadow-sm [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
            <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer font-bold text-zinc-950 text-base">
              <span>What is the Ohio Maneuverability Test and do you practice it?</span>
              <span class="ml-4 flex-shrink-0 transition duration-300 group-open:-rotate-180 text-orange-600">
                <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
              </span>
            </summary>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed border-t border-zinc-100 pt-3">
              The Ohio maneuverability test is a two-part test required on the state road exam consisting of driving forward through a 9-by-20 foot box, steering to the right or left of a point marker, stopping parallel, and then backing through the course without hitting any cones or stopping unnecessarily. <strong>We practice this extensively during our behind-the-wheel sessions using exact BMV cone measurements.</strong>
            </p>
          </details>

          <details class="group bg-white p-5 rounded-2xl border border-zinc-200 shadow-sm [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
            <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer font-bold text-zinc-950 text-base">
              <span>Do adults (over 18) have to take a full driving school course?</span>
              <span class="ml-4 flex-shrink-0 transition duration-300 group-open:-rotate-180 text-orange-600">
                <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
              </span>
            </summary>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed border-t border-zinc-100 pt-3">
              Adults 18 and older are not strictly required by Ohio law to complete a teen course before taking the driving test for the first time. However, if an adult fails the road test on their first attempt, Ohio requires an <strong>Abbreviated Adult Course</strong> before retesting. Additionally, many adults choose our private lessons to gain crucial confidence and pass on their first try!
            </p>
          </details>

          <details class="group bg-white p-5 rounded-2xl border border-zinc-200 shadow-sm [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
            <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer font-bold text-zinc-950 text-base">
              <span>What vehicles are used for the behind-the-wheel lessons?</span>
              <span class="ml-4 flex-shrink-0 transition duration-300 group-open:-rotate-180 text-orange-600">
                <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
              </span>
            </summary>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed border-t border-zinc-100 pt-3">
              All behind-the-wheel training is conducted in our modern, well-maintained school fleet equipped with <strong>state-certified dual passenger brakes</strong>, auxiliary rear-view mirrors, and commercial driving school insurance for maximum student safety.
            </p>
          </details>

        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

